Title: Moong Dal Chilla Recipe

Channel: vegrecipesofindia.com

Linked recipe blog structured data (schema.org Recipe JSON-LD) — prefer this for method text when it has instructions:

{
  "@type": "Recipe",
  "name": "Moong Dal Chilla Recipe",
  "author": {
    "@type": "Person",
    "name": "Dassana Amit"
  },
  "description": "Moong Dal Chilla is a savory Indian pancake prepared with soaked and ground yellow moong lentils. The batter is seasoned with onions, herbs and spices before being cooked on a skillet. Serve them hot with green chutney or yogurt for breakfast or brunch.",
  "datePublished": "2022-07-06T21:19:35+00:00",
  "image": [
    "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/11/moong-dal-chilla-3u.jpg",
    "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/11/moong-dal-chilla-3u-500x500.jpg",
    "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/11/moong-dal-chilla-3u-500x375.jpg",
    "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/11/moong-dal-chilla-3u-480x270.jpg"
  ],
  "recipeYield": [
    "12",
    "12 Moong Dal Chilla"
  ],
  "prepTime": "PT240M",
  "cookTime": "PT30M",
  "totalTime": "PT270M",
  "recipeIngredient": [
    "1 cup moong dal ((split &amp; husked yellow moong lentils))",
    "2 to 3 cups water (– for soaking)",
    "¼ cup water (– for grinding lentils or add as required)",
    "¼ teaspoon turmeric powder",
    "¼ teaspoon red chili powder (or cayenne pepper)",
    "½ teaspoon roasted cumin powder ( or cumin powder (ground cumin))",
    "1 pinch hing ((asafoetida), optional)",
    "¼ cup coriander leaves (– chopped (cilantro))",
    "¼ cup onions (– finely chopped)",
    "1 teaspoon grated ginger (or finely chopped ginger)",
    "1 to 2 or ½ to 1 teaspoon  green chilies (– finely chopped)",
    "1 teaspoon salt (or add as required)",
    "2 to 3 tablespoons oil (– for cooking chilla or add as required)"
  ],
  "recipeInstructions": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToSection",
      "name": "Soaking &amp; Grinding Moong Dal",
      "itemListElement": [
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Rinse the moong dal 3 to 4 times in water.",
          "name": "Rinse the moong dal 3 to 4 times in water.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/moong-dal-chilla-recipe/#wprm-recipe-139150-step-0-0"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Soak the lentils with 2 to 3 cups of water for 3 to 4 hours or overnight if you plan to make the chilla for breakfast.",
          "name": "Soak the lentils with 2 to 3 cups of water for 3 to 4 hours or overnight if you plan to make the chilla for breakfast.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/moong-dal-chilla-recipe/#wprm-recipe-139150-step-0-1"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "The moong dal will swell or double up in size. Discard the water. Rinse the mung lentils again a few times in water. Drain all the water.",
          "name": "The moong dal will swell or double up in size. Discard the water. Rinse the mung lentils again a few times in water. Drain all the water.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/moong-dal-chilla-recipe/#wprm-recipe-139150-step-0-2"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "In a grinder, add the soaked moong lentils and ¼ cup of water. Grind to a smooth and fine consistency.",
          "name": "In a grinder, add the soaked moong lentils and ¼ cup of water. Grind to a smooth and fine consistency.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/moong-dal-chilla-recipe/#wprm-recipe-139150-step-0-3"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Don&#039;t add too much water as the lentils might not grind evenly. We need a smooth and lump free batter for moong dal chilla.",
          "name": "Don&#039;t add too much water as the lentils might not grind evenly. We need a smooth and lump free batter for moong dal chilla.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/moong-dal-chilla-recipe/#wprm-recipe-139150-step-0-4"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToSection",
      "name": "Seasoning Batter",
      "itemListElement": [
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Take the finely ground batter in a bowl. Add turmeric powder, red chili powder, cumin powder and salt or as required.",
          "name": "Take the finely ground batter in a bowl. Add turmeric powder, red chili powder, cumin powder and salt or as required.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/moong-dal-chilla-recipe/#wprm-recipe-139150-step-1-0"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Mix very well.&nbsp;",
          "name": "Mix very well.&nbsp;",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/moong-dal-chilla-recipe/#wprm-recipe-139150-step-1-1"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Then add the chopped coriander leaves, chopped onions, grated ginger, finely chopped green chilies and a pinch of asafoetida. ",
          "name": "Then add the chopped coriander leaves, chopped onions, grated ginger, finely chopped green chilies and a pinch of asafoetida. ",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/moong-dal-chilla-recipe/#wprm-recipe-139150-step-1-2"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Again mix very well.&nbsp;",
          "name": "Again mix very well.&nbsp;",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/moong-dal-chilla-recipe/#wprm-recipe-139150-step-1-3"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Allow the batter to rest for 15 to 20 mins.",
          "name": "Allow the batter to rest for 15 to 20 mins.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/moong-dal-chilla-recipe/#wprm-recipe-139150-step-1-4"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "The onions will leave some moisture. Check the consistency of the batter. If its too thick, then add 1 to 2 tablespoons more water. But remember not to add too much of water as the batter will not spread evenly on the skillet or tawa.",
          "name": "The onions will leave some moisture. Check the consistency of the batter. If its too thick, then add 1 to 2 tablespoons more water. But remember not to add too much of water as the batter will not spread evenly on the skillet or tawa.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/moong-dal-chilla-recipe/#wprm-recipe-139150-step-1-5"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "The consistency of the batter has to be of pouring consistency, neither too thick nor too thin.",
          "name": "The consistency of the batter has to be of pouring consistency, neither too thick nor too thin.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/moong-dal-chilla-recipe/#wprm-recipe-139150-step-1-6"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToSection",
      "name": "Making Moong Dal Chilla",
      "itemListElement": [
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Heat a well seasoned pan. This is important as the pan has to be hot before you make the cheelas.If using a cast iron pan, spread ½ teaspoon of oil evenly on the pan.If using a non-stick pan, do not spread oil on it.",
          "name": "Heat a well seasoned pan. This is important as the pan has to be hot before you make the cheelas.If using a cast iron pan, spread ½ teaspoon of oil evenly on the pan.If using a non-stick pan, do not spread oil on it.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/moong-dal-chilla-recipe/#wprm-recipe-139150-step-2-0"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Add a scoopful of batter towards the center of the pan.",
          "name": "Add a scoopful of batter towards the center of the pan.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/moong-dal-chilla-recipe/#wprm-recipe-139150-step-2-1"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "The batter will spread a little on its own.",
          "name": "The batter will spread a little on its own.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/moong-dal-chilla-recipe/#wprm-recipe-139150-step-2-2"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Just rotate the batter with the back of spatula giving a round and even shape.",
          "name": "Just rotate the batter with the back of spatula giving a round and even shape.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/moong-dal-chilla-recipe/#wprm-recipe-139150-step-2-3"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Cook the chilla on medium heat. After a minute they will look crisp and brown from the bottom.",
          "name": "Cook the chilla on medium heat. After a minute they will look crisp and brown from the bottom.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/moong-dal-chilla-recipe/#wprm-recipe-139150-step-2-4"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "At this point drizzle a bit of oil around the edges and in the center of the chilla. Spread the oil drops with a spoon all over the cooked chilla.",
          "name": "At this point drizzle a bit of oil around the edges and in the center of the chilla. Spread the oil drops with a spoon all over the cooked chilla.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/moong-dal-chilla-recipe/#wprm-recipe-139150-step-2-5"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Flip the chilla and cook the other side for a minute.",
          "name": "Flip the chilla and cook the other side for a minute.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/moong-dal-chilla-recipe/#wprm-recipe-139150-step-2-6"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Once the moong dal chilla appear crisp and golden, remove and place aside. ",
          "name": "Once the moong dal chilla appear crisp and golden, remove and place aside. ",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/moong-dal-chilla-recipe/#wprm-recipe-139150-step-2-7"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Similarly make all other chilla. You can opt to stuff the chilla with some grated paneer if you want. ",
          "name": "Similarly make all other chilla. You can opt to stuff the chilla with some grated paneer if you want. ",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/moong-dal-chilla-recipe/#wprm-recipe-139150-step-2-8"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Serve moong dal chilla with tomato ketchup or green chutney.",
          "name": "Serve moong dal chilla with tomato ketchup or green chutney.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/moong-dal-chilla-recipe/#wprm-recipe-139150-step-2-9"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
